# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession draft Blacksmithing --out` from Forever's client tables, trainer lists and data/forever. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/blacksmithing
title Blacksmithing 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Blacksmithing hammers bars into plate and mail, weapons, keys, rods, and the sharpening, weight
# and grinding stones the later recipes eat. Mining is its partner: every bar is smelted from ore,
# and the stones come straight from the veins. A Blacksmith Hammer must be in your bags, and almost
# every recipe needs an anvil (towns and forges have them).
#
# Forever's changes: almost every plan was moved 25 points down. It turns yellow, green and grey 25
# points sooner, and trainers teach it 25 points earlier (Runed Copper Belt from 45, Heavy Grinding
# Stone from 100), so a Classic route crafts grey recipes in about nine places. Copper Rod (for
# enchanters) is now Blacksmithing. Many new plans arrive in sets keyed to a gem or dust; most of
# them are sold for Merchant's Favor by Gor'mak near the Crossroads and Stondry Darkhammer at Three
# Corners (Redridge), and their later pieces need Sandpaper (Engineering) and Sulfuric Acid
# (Alchemy). Merchant's Favor is a currency from the supply crates turned in at the camps, not gold;
# its patterns bind when picked up. This route leaves them out.
#
# Camping: Sharpening Wheel (skill 20) is the Blacksmithing camp item. The Anvil (skill 140) is a
# camp station from a blueprint Gilnid drops in the Deadmines. The skill-300 Master Forge has no
# known blueprint source, and about 60 late plans need it.
#
# Ranks: Journeyman needs character level 10 (Forever's sniffed lists). Expert is taught only by
# Bengus Deepforge (Ironforge), Saru Steelfury (Orgrimmar) and Brikk Keencraft (Booty Bay); Artisan
# only by Brikk Keencraft. Specialisation at 200 and level 40: Armorsmith (Grumnus Steelshaper,
# Ironforge / Okothos Ironrager, Orgrimmar) or Weaponsmith (Ironus Coldsteel, Ironforge / Borgosh
# Corebender, Orgrimmar), with the axe, hammer and sword masters in Everlook at 250 and level 50.
#
# Route (crafts are expected counts; yellow and green crafts can take more):
#     1-35  Rough Sharpening Stone, about 42 (known): 1 Rough Stone each
#    35-75  Rough Grinding Stone, about 64 (trainer 1s): 2 Rough Stone each
#    75-83  Rough Grinding Stone, about 58 (trainer 1s): 2 Rough Stone each
#    83-100 Runed Copper Belt, about 21 (trainer 2s): 10 Copper Bar each
#   100-113 Heavy Sharpening Stone, about 28 (trainer 10s): 1 Heavy Stone each
#   113-150 Patterned Bronze Bracers, about 64 (trainer 5s): 5 Bronze Bar and 2 Coarse Grinding Stone each
#   150-175 Green Iron Bracers, about 28 (trainer): 6 Iron Bar and 1 Green Dye each
#   175-185 Solid Sharpening Stone, about 30 (trainer): 1 Solid Stone each
#   185-205 Golden Scale Bracers, about 39 (trainer): 5 Steel Bar and 2 Heavy Grinding Stone each
#   205-225 Heavy Mithril Breastplate, about 20 (trainer): 16 Mithril Bar each
#   225-235 Dense Weightstone, about 17 (trainer): 1 Dense Stone each
#   235-247 Heavy Mithril Boots, about 30 (trainer): 14 Mithril Bar and 4 Thick Leather each
#   247-250 Big Black Mace, about 11 (trainer): 16 Mithril Bar, 1 Black Pearl, 4 Shadowgem, 1 Solid Grinding Stone and 2 Thick Leather each
#   250-255 Ornate Thorium Handaxe, about 5 (recipe 1g 60s): 20 Thorium Bar, 2 Large Opal, 2 Dense Grinding Stone and 4 Rugged Leather each
#   255-285 Huge Thorium Battleaxe, about 31 (recipe 2g): 40 Thorium Bar, 6 Dense Grinding Stone and 6 Rugged Leather each
#   285-300 Imperial Plate Boots, about 19 (quest, 40 Thorium Bar): 34 Thorium Bar, 1 Star Ruby and 1 Aquamarine each
#
# Shopping per bracket (vendor goods at vendor prices; gathered or dropped materials by count):
# 1-75: Apprentice 10c, recipes 1s; gather or buy 286 Rough Stone.
# 75-150: Journeyman 5s, recipes 19s 50c, vendor goods 18c; gather or buy 256 Coarse Stone, 28 Heavy
# Stone, 210 Copper Bar and 320 Bronze Bar.
# 150-225: Expert 50s (Classic price), recipes 10s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 28s;
# gather or buy 234 Heavy Stone, 168 Iron Bar, 195 Steel Bar, 320 Mithril Bar and 30 Solid Stone.
# 225-300: Artisan 5g (Classic price), recipes 3g 60s plus unpriced trainer recipes; gather or buy
# 44 Shadowgem, 596 Mithril Bar, 142 Thick Leather, 19 Aquamarine, 19 Star Ruby, 44 Solid Stone, 11
# Black Pearl, 206 Rugged Leather, 2026 Thorium Bar, 801 Dense Stone and 10 Large Opal.
#
# Data: recipes, colours and reagents from the Forever client's tables; trainer learn skills and
# prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists (they reach skill 50-150); vendors, stock and drops
# from data/forever. Materials are valued at about four times their vendor sell price (cloth and
# leather by the square root of it, hides four times higher; tools/lib/professions/materials.js) to
# rank recipes against each other, never as a price forecast.
# ASSUMED: learn skills of Green Iron Bracers 140, Solid Sharpening Stone 175, Golden Scale Bracers
# 160, Heavy Mithril Breastplate 205, Dense Weightstone 225, Heavy Mithril Boots 210, Solid Grinding
# Stone 175, Big Black Mace 205 and Dense Grinding Stone 225 (no sniffed Forever list teaches them:
# Classic's trainer skill moved as far as Forever moved the recipe's colours, which the sniffed
# lists bear out on 126 of 129 recipes). In-game check: the skill the trainer asks; their prices are
# not in the data.
# ASSUMED: rank level gates Expert 20 and Artisan 35 (Classic's; Forever's sniffed lists ask level 1
# for Apprentice and 10 for Journeyman). In-game check: the level each trainer asks.
# ASSUMED: Derotain Mudsipper's Imperial Plate quests ask Blacksmithing 265 and character level 50
# (Forever's quest data, as in Classic, though Forever moved the plans themselves 25 points down to
# 240-270). In-game check: the skill his quests ask; a lower one lets the Imperial Plate Bracers
# (orange to 265) take over from the battleaxe sooner.
# ASSUMED: rank prices Expert 50s and Artisan 5g (Classic's trainer lists; Forever's sniffed lists
# price only Apprentice 10c and Journeyman 5s, as in Classic). In-game check: what Expert and
# Artisan cost.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice (1-75)
section Blacksmithing 1-75

step Learn Blacksmithing
  tip Apprentice Blacksmithing lets you craft up to 75 for 10c, at any character level. Any Blacksmithing trainer of your faction teaches it; the arrow picks the nearest. Buy a Blacksmith Hammer (any blacksmithing supplier) and pair it with Mining: Rough Stone and Copper Ore come from the Copper Veins of every starting zone. 1-75 takes about 1s of recipes, plus 286 Rough Stone to gather or buy.
  train Blacksmithing Apprentice
  skill Blacksmithing 1

