step Green Iron Bracers to 175
  zone Azeroth
  tip Green Iron Bracers is orange at 150 (yellow 165, green 177, grey 190): about 28 crafts to 175. Each takes 6 Iron Bar and 1 Green Dye. Six Iron Bars and a Green Dye a craft; Green Dye comes from tailoring, leatherworking and trade supplies vendors. Orange to 165 on Forever, so a point every craft for the first fifteen. Needs an anvil nearby. Iron Bar (168 for 150-225): Mining: smelt Iron Ore; or the Auction House.
  craft 3501 until 175

step Blacksmithing recipes at 175
  tip Back to a Blacksmithing trainer: Solid Sharpening Stone (from 175).
  learn 9918

step Solid Sharpening Stone to 185
  tip Solid Sharpening Stone is yellow at 175 (yellow 175, green 180, grey 185): about 30 crafts to 185. Each takes 1 Solid Stone. One Solid Stone a craft (Mithril Deposits): cheap points between the iron and the steel bracers. Use the stones on your weapons or sell them.
  craft 9918 until 185

step Blacksmithing recipes at 185
  tip Back to a Blacksmithing trainer: Golden Scale Bracers (from 160).
  learn 7223

step Golden Scale Bracers to 205
  tip Golden Scale Bracers is yellow at 185 (yellow 185, green 197, grey 210): about 39 crafts to 205. Each takes 5 Steel Bar and 2 Heavy Grinding Stone. Make the 78 Heavy Grinding Stone first. Steel Bars are smelted from an Iron Bar and a Coal (Mining 165; Coal from trade and blacksmithing suppliers), so each bracer is five of each. Each bracer takes two Heavy Grinding Stones: make them first. Specialisation (optional): at 200 and character level 40, Grumnus Steelshaper (Ironforge) or Okothos Ironrager (Orgrimmar) starts The Art of the Armorsmith: 4 Ornate Mithril Helms, 2 Ornate Mithril Boots and an Ornate Mithril Breastplate, whose plans come from a Mithril Order quest chain. Ironus Coldsteel (Ironforge) or Borgosh Corebender (Orgrimmar) starts The Way of the Weaponsmith: 4 Moonsteel Broadswords, 4 Massive Iron Axes, 2 Heavy Mithril Axes and 2 Big Black Maces; on Forever the Moonsteel Broadsword plans (Zarena Cromwind, Booty Bay) and Massive Iron Axe plans bind when picked up, so buy and use them yourself. You can take only one; neither is needed for 300, and the beta never tested them (it stopped at level 30). Needs an anvil nearby. Steel Bar (195 for 150-225): Mining: smelt Iron Bar and Coal; or the Auction House.
  craft 3337 x78
  craft 7223 until 205

step Blacksmithing recipes at 205
  tip Back to a Blacksmithing trainer: Heavy Mithril Breastplate (from 205).
  learn 9959

step Heavy Mithril Breastplate to 225
  tip Heavy Mithril Breastplate is orange at 205 (yellow 225, green 235, grey 245): about 20 crafts to 225, a point every craft. Each takes 16 Mithril Bar. Sixteen Mithril Bars a craft and nothing else; orange to 225 on Forever, so a point every craft to the Artisan cap. Needs an anvil nearby. Mithril Bar (320 for 150-225): Mining: smelt Mithril Ore; or the Auction House. Blacksmithing 225 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 9959 until 225
  skill Blacksmithing 225

